    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_method_starts_precise_definition_dow",
          "text": "The method starts from a precise definition of down-scaling: ideal downsampling, which first applies an ideal low-pass filter that zeros out all frequencies above the new Nyquist limit, then subsamples.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "method",
            "starts",
            "precise",
            "definition",
            "down-scaling",
            "ideal",
            "downsampling",
            "which",
            "first",
            "applies"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_authors_derive_their_central_conditi",
          "text": "From this the authors derive their central condition, Claim 1: a deep net is truly scale-equivariant if and only if every output frequency term depends only on input frequency terms that are equal or lower.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "authors",
            "derive",
            "their",
            "central",
            "condition",
            "claim",
            "1",
            "deep",
            "net",
            "truly"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_they_redesign_network_component_sati",
          "text": "They then redesign each network component to satisfy this rule. A spatially-local Fourier layer constrains the kernel so it learns local features while staying equivariant. A scale-equivariant non-linearity applies ReLU frequency-band by frequency-band. A Fourier pooling layer preserves the same dependency structure.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "they",
            "redesign",
            "network",
            "component",
            "satisfy",
            "rule",
            "spatially-local",
            "fourier",
            "layer",
            "constrains"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_top_equivariant_feature_extractor_th",
          "text": "On top of the equivariant feature extractor, they add a classifier that predicts once per scale, sharing a single MLP across scales through Fourier padding, and train it with a hinge consistency loss that penalizes the model whenever a higher-resolution image is predicted worse than its lower-resolution version.",
          "expected_role": "figure",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "top",
            "equivariant",
            "feature",
            "extractor",
            "they",
            "add",
            "classifier",
            "predicts",
            "once",
            "per"
          ],
