          "anchor_id": "cue_s09_c2_once_you_formulate_down_scaling_idea",
          "text": "Once you formulate down-scaling as ideal, anti-aliased downsampling and require every output frequency to depend only on equal or lower input frequencies, you can build networks from Fourier layers that are exactly scale-equivariant, with provably zero error rather than the small residual errors that plagued earlier methods.",
